// Plan stage R0z Z9c-B (R-VREF, review round 2, B3 and B4; the bad twin):
// a reference can be live in the window of the task, so the call keeps the
// rule of main. The probe of the review:
// Review probe Z9c-B r2 (R-VREF edge): the reference is a value of a type parameter `T` of `par`; `par`
// holds it across the call of `f`, whose task `h` pushes to `w`.
fn par<T>(h: fn(), x: T, show: fn(T)) / async {
    let f = || scope { s => s.spawn(h); () }
    f()
    show(x)
}
fn main() / async {
    let w = Vec.new()
    w.push(1)
    par(|| w.push(2), &w[0], |y: &u64| print(y))
}
